#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:5 e740f5972a11417981012e836b3358c3
msgid "Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:7 20963a5ec43b4ff18cd09cb3e53107d3
msgid ""
"The battery failsafe can be configured to automatically switch the "
"vehicle into :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>`, :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` or "
":ref:`Land <land-mode>` mode if the vehicle battery voltage drops below a"
" specified voltage for 10 seconds or the estimated remaining capacity has"
" dropped below a configurable threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:11 5a9b17a6d6f146f6b1782f829e5dafc9
msgid ""
"This failsafe requires the vehicle have a working :ref:`Power Module "
"<common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:13 f672aae5766744de8fee30947b0b5444
msgid ""
"ArduPilot firmware versions 4.0 and later support up to 9 batteries/power"
" monitors. The discussion below applies to those optional batteries also."
" Each can trigger a failsafe and each can have different actions and "
"setup values. In addition, a group of batteries can be treated as a "
"single unit, see ``BATTx_MONITOR`` = 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:16 7cc8740b8b6f4913b2e1ce6de8261ccd
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:18 4370f9f113654a93b18e9c21d39bd9f2
msgid ""
"If enabled and set-up correctly the battery failsafe will trigger if the "
"main battery's"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:20 71f2c47689fe4babaaeecde1bae1ddc7
msgid ""
"voltage drops below the voltage held in the :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT "
"<BATT_LOW_VOLT>` parameter (or FS_BATT_VOLTAGE in older versions) for "
"more than 10 seconds. The default voltage is 10.5 volts. If set to zero, "
"the voltage based trigger will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:21 987f6ba989d045b6b6f4da3a291cb887
#, python-format
msgid ""
"remaining capacity falls below the :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` "
"parameter (or FS_BATT_MAH in older versions) 20% of the battery's full "
"capacity is a good choice (i.e. \"1000\" for a 5000mAh battery). If set "
"to zero, the capacity based trigger will be disabled (i.e. only voltage "
"will be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:24 3c0f051c46524476a2ac7449649a3b11
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:26 636d858d06564147a62e57310a7be160
msgid "When the failsafe is triggered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:28 8ab25e3e25dc4d868df6725b8e63ef90
msgid "Buzzer will play a loud low-battery alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:29 347e010ff57942c9aed1cb8ae4c304bf
msgid "LEDs will flash yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:30 3388fd56f3994ab78a42840a970d228f
msgid ""
"\"Low Battery!\" will be displayed on the ground stations HUD (if "
"telemetry is connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:32 d8eac04626c8464aad090e959cd8bb86
msgid "Then one of the following will happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:34 3f58027cdd7d4915a4e3d216b3d56f05
msgid "**Nothing** if the vehicle is already disarmed or executing RTL or Land"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:35 0eae7fe50091418b81d2a72fd0a74156
msgid ""
"**Disarm motors** if the vehicle is in Stabilize or Acro mode and the "
"throttle is at zero OR the vehicle is landed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:36 bf8a5479e25542b6aae2129e5f6d8c12
msgid ""
"The user configurable action held in the :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT "
"<BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:38 7d6cee6f9eeb490eb4f38c4c2ed8251b
msgid "**0** : None - no action will be taken"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:39 20e97fe59b6d4918af3dfbfc33e2f42b
msgid "**1** : Land - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:40 b6da5edb4f8b45dea1397ed6ea0e4248
msgid ""
"**2** : RTL - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Return-to-Launch <rtl-"
"mode>` mode if possible but if not possible (because of no good position "
"estimate) the vehicle will :ref:`Land <land-mode>` (**Recommended**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:41 f603aa9b997f46a28f7121c2c53b73d0
msgid ""
"**3** : SmartRTL or RTL - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`SmartRTL "
"<smartrtl-mode>` mode if possible, if not possible (because SmartRTL's "
"position buffer is full) the vehicle will switch to :ref:`RTL <rtl-"
"mode>`. If RTL is also not possible (because of no good position "
"estimate) the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:42 defa4103f90b455087e03ec8290a3eea
msgid ""
"**4** : SmartRTL or Land - the vehicle will switch to :ref:`SmartRTL "
"<smartrtl-mode>` mode if possible, if not possible (because SmartRTL's "
"position buffer is full) the vehicle will switch to :ref:`Land <land-"
"mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:43 250a95a568af4d388d47fcad54b5f796
msgid ""
"**5** : Terminate - the vehicle will disarm the motors. This is a "
"dangerous option that should not be used in most cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:44 e7db3ee7f89e4672a94579af2326f632
msgid ""
"**6** : Auto DO_LAND_START or RTL - the vehicle will jump to the nearest "
"\"DO_LAND_START\" mission item or RTL if no \"DO_LAND_START\" mission "
"item has been programmed (see :ref:`common-do-land-start`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:45 2cd77655449444b48338cb2750847ac7
msgid ""
"**7** : Switch to :ref:`Brake mode <brake-mode>` if it can, otherwise, "
"switch to :ref:`Land <land-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:47 b6834e06c5644b418552cc7b679d5400
msgid ""
"As with all failsafes, the user can re-take control of the vehicle by "
"changing the flight mode switch to another mode. The battery failsafe "
"will not trigger again unless the two-layer failsafe is setup (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:49 49fd9b597fce43258b148ac8ce7de177
msgid ""
"The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` parameter (Copter 4.0 and later) is a "
"bitmask parameter to select one or more options that modify the standard "
"actions of the radio, GCS, and battery failsafe. In the Mission Planner "
"full parameter list or full parameter tree, the handy checkbox popup "
"window is an easy way to set this (and any other bitmask) parameter. Be "
"sure to go to Help > Check Beta Updates to pull the latest parameter "
"definitions first while connected to the internet. The "
":ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` bits are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:51 bda8bcffddc94f43a4a76eb5a42249e6
msgid ""
"bit 0 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-"
"failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:52 fa50037e92ba46429ba73ae53ec581a1
msgid ""
"bit 1 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Ground Control Station "
"Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:53 0cdb5b1ff10c4516ab954ff9c901b28b
msgid ""
"bit 2 set: Continue if in guided mode :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-"
"failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:54 52b300b3d0d9409aac635358f780738d
msgid "bit 3 set: Continue if landing on any failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:55 6fc33df919f74d04a4e4bc2cdb7f32d7
msgid ""
"bit 4 set: Continue in pilot control on :ref:`Ground Control Station "
"Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:56 755f58a6afa3494293dbcff539094dce
msgid ""
"if none of the above are set, then execute the :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT "
"<BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` or :ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` options as"
" configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:58 6a7ad6773cc5443d9afe74b16c8025a9
msgid ""
"Only bitmask bit 3 affects actions taken during Battery failsafe. This "
"parameter also works in conjunction with the GCS and radio failsafe, so "
"ensure you are taking all options into account when setting this "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:62 65e1a17e5aba4852ad12e4941624f175
msgid ""
"Even if the failsafe action is set to \"None\" (i.e. "
":ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 0) the buzzer will buzz and "
"the LEDs will flash yellow. To completely disable the battery failsafe "
"set :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` and :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH "
"<BATT_LOW_MAH>` to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:66 b113a0cf90924c35a0d9dc485064c4d1
msgid ""
"Once the battery failsafe has triggered, it cannot be reset until the "
"autopilot is rebooted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:69 50ee6ad1fb6e4a8ca2dff07701bca23c
msgid "Setting up using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:71 386e07c8406247359aea89753846d924
msgid "On the **INITIAL SETUP \\| Mandatory Hardware \\| Failsafe** page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:73 051a59d238534b7a9e2d2e93df9a368c
msgid ""
"If the Battery section parameters are greyed out follow instructions to "
"setup the :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:74 e0a94c552de7474781d5c83a0914f0d1
msgid "Set the \"Low Battery\" threshold voltage (i.e. 10.5 volts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:75 c5b44f8c27a04cb392b00e957977d1e3
msgid ""
"Set the \"Reserved MAH\" or leave as \"0\" if the failsafe should never "
"trigger based on estimated current consumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:76 102e07a471b24c87883f2564eb197935
msgid ""
"Select the desired behavior (Land, RTL, SmartRTL, etc) from the drop-down"
" list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:82 8495fe0bca014264bbec1b6e937a337d
msgid "Two-Layer failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:84 20b11da02b03446eab86fb089e998942
msgid ""
"ArduPilot includes a two-layer battery failsafe. This allows setting up a"
" follow-up action if the battery voltage or remaining capacity falls "
"below an even lower threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:86 a03e04a4231c4132bc7245bf476fbd60
msgid ""
":ref:`BATT_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` - holds the secondary (lower) "
"voltage threshold. Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:87 a023f7580582411da446dd360411a74f
msgid ""
":ref:`BATT_CRT_MAH <BATT_CRT_MAH>` - holds the secondary (lower) capacity"
" threshold. Set to zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:88 bc095eacd0084e979516728afc2fad6a
msgid ""
":ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` - holds the secondary action to "
"take. A reasonable setup would be to have :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT "
"<BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 2 (RTL) and :ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>`"
" = 1 (Land)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:91 73382de214e54c7eb93157be8b6248b0
msgid "Advanced Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:93 bb82421fd3d24381875f1feecffa1189
msgid ""
":ref:`BATT_FS_VOLTSRC <BATT_FS_VOLTSRC>` allows configuring whether the "
"raw battery voltage or a sag corrected voltage is used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:94 25dd3a9dfe1841599b9d9013fa34dad8
msgid ""
":ref:`BATT_LOW_TIMER <BATT_LOW_TIMER>` can configure how long the voltage"
" must be below the threshold for the failsafe to trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/failsafe-battery.rst:95 8a34f6c8aa3c4571abe7c5160e942f4d
msgid ""
"``BATTx_`` parameters can be setup to trigger the failsafe on other "
"batteries"
msgstr ""

